## Task 2 — Snapshot Creation & Restoration

### Implementation Overview

- handles Tomcat stop/start, DB connection cleanup.
- `/snapshot/create` endpoint triggers `Core.checkpointRestore()`.
- CLI tool implemented to trigger snapshot/restore commands.
- Minimal subset captured: fully initialized Spring context, Tomcat, HikariCP pool.
- Optimal snapshot time selected: warmed, idle system.


### CRaC Snapshots Cannot Be Created on Windows

CRaC requires:
- Linux kernel features (checkpoint_restore syscall)
- CRIU
- A Linux JVM distribution with CRaC support

Attempts made:

| Environment | Result |
|------------|---------|
| Windows native | Cannot checkpoint |
| Docker Desktop + WSL2 | I never managed to make it work properly. snapshots were never generated |
| Linux VM | My PC struggled to run VM |
:/
In ideal situation i would use existing scripts to measure cold and snapshot start time and take average over 5 runs.
also simulation traffic with curl + bash script as extra
